.TH SET_MEMPOLICY 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
set_mempolicy \- Linux x86-64 syscall 238
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B long set_mempolicy(int mode, const unsigned long* nodes, unsigned long maxnode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the calling thread's NUMA policy.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR set_mempolicy (2)
